# Core Standards

Coding standards for the PioneerDJCorrector project. All code must adhere to these principles for consistency, maintainability, and quality.

## Clean, Reusable, Modular Code

- Organize code in small, single-purpose functions and components with clear names
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Reuse utilities and patterns. New code should be generic enough to be reused

## Edit Carefully

- Read and understand files before editing
- Preserve working behavior unless change is agreed
- Refactor in minimal, focused changes

## Adherence

Adhere to all rules on every task. If a rule must be broken, explicitly call out why and record rationale/impact in `docs/technical_decisions.md`.
